Chapter: GpuEffect
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceBuffer
  cites Gpu chapter LaunchConfig

 The Gpu effect marks host-side code that launches kernels and moves
 buffers. A function with Gpu in its effect row talks to the GPU but
 does not run on it. The Device effect (in DeviceEffect.codex) marks
 code that runs on the GPU itself.

 We say:

Section: Definitions

  effect Gpu where
    gpu-init              : [Gpu] Integer
    gpu-load-ptx          : Text -> [Gpu] Integer
    gpu-alloc             : Integer -> [Gpu] Integer
    gpu-free              : Integer -> [Gpu] Nothing
    gpu-copy-to           : Integer, List Integer -> [Gpu] Nothing
    gpu-copy-from         : Integer, Integer -> [Gpu] List Integer
    gpu-launch            : Text, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> [Gpu] Integer
    gpu-sync              : [Gpu] Nothing
    gpu-available          : [Gpu] Integer
    gpu-error             : [Gpu] Text
    kernel-launch         : KernelDescriptor, LaunchConfig, List DeviceArg -> [Gpu.Compute] Nothing

